# Only the files the pipeline actually reads are tracked, because these are
# plain git blobs (no LFS) and every rebuild rewrites them into history.
#
#   <group>_mito_refdb.fasta        GetOrganelle reseed seed (-s), and the
#                                   BLAST subject for reference selection  -> tracked
#   <group>_mito_refdb.label.fasta  GetOrganelle label database (--genes)   -> tracked
#   <group>_mito_refdb.manifest.tsv organism, family, taxonomy lineage      -> tracked
#   <group>_mito_refdb.features.tsv feature types and exon coordinates      -> tracked
#   <group>_mito_refdb.gb           build intermediate only, 84 MB across
#                                   the groups; bin/refdb_record.py rebuilds
#                                   an equivalent record from the four
#                                   tracked files above                     -> never tracked
#   <group>_mito_refdb.nucl.*       BLAST db, rebuilt on demand             -> never tracked
#
# Regenerate the .gb (and with it any group's derived files) with
#   bin/build_invert_reference_db.py --group <group> --email <you>
# or, to refresh the derived files from an existing .gb without re-querying
# NCBI and thereby changing which records the database holds,
#   bin/build_invert_reference_db.py --group <group> --refresh-derived
*_mito_refdb.gb
*_mito_refdb.nucl.*
